<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<xmsbt>
<entry label="tip_title_3200">
<text>Thwomp</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3200">
<text>First appearing in Super Mario Bros. 3, Thwomps appear as an angry living
stone suspended in the air. Waiting until a certain mustache'd hero walks
closely nearby, before attempting to crush the intruder!</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_title_3201">
<text>Thwomp: Attributes</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3201">
<text>Thwomp as fighter can be a formidable force, having good defense, even
with a lack of high speed! And although his air mobility might also lack a bit,
getting hit by him might really make the difference!</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_title_3202">
<text>Thwimps</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3202">
<text>Having first appeared in Super Mario World, the smaller, less impactful,
and almost child-like Thwimps makes an appearence in Thwomp's second victory!
It's really cute! I wonder if there might be another taunt they appear in...
</text>
</entry>

<entry label="tip_title_3203">
<text>Thwomp: Ground Smash (Neutral Special)</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3203">
<text>The ever so iconic attack! Thwomp will lift off from the ground and then strike down!
Holding the special button delays his slam, but increases his damage output!
A midair use of this move comes out quicker but with a consistant attack power.</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_title_3204">
<text>Thwomp: Wall Slam (Side Special)</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3204">
<text>In recent times, there have been Thwomps known for slaming sideways!
Like vertical ones, there's no stopping his momentum! If he hits a ledge,
he might cause a bit of a ground shake, damaging any nearby foes!</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_title_3205">
<text>Thwomp: Thwimp (Up Special)</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3205">
<text>Thwimps don't act like Thwomps do. They hop back and forth. With this
in mind, Thwomp will also perform a huge jump, before slamming from a great
height! You can even control which direction he moves in!</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_title_3206">
<text>Thwomp: Angry Powerup (Down Special)</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3206">
<text>Thwomp can absorb an impact in anger to increase his own power!
A lighter hit or a stronger attack will determine the temporary state of anger he goes into!
</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_title_3207">
<text>Thwomp: Mega Form (Final Smash)</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3207">
<text>A huge Thwomp falls from a great height! If he reaches the end of
the screen, he will reappear up top for 2 more times! You can even
choose how right or leftward he'll reappear using the control stick!
</text>
</entry>

<entry label="tip_title_3208">
<text>Thwomp: Side Attack</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3208">
<text>Thwomp's side attack pays a particular reference to another certain enemy.
All he does is fall flat fowards though.. Really? I mean, who does that?
</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_title_3209">
<text>Thwomp: Down Attack</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3209">
<text>Thwomp's down attack has him rollout for a small distance. Quite the attack!
Specifically, he won't roll off the ledge in most circumstances, but he can if
there's ground nearby!
</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_title_3210">
<text>Thwomp: Win 3</text>
</entry>
<entry label="tip_text_3210">
<text>In Thwomp's 3rd win screen, Mario appears, and gets taken out by Thwomp!
If Luigi is in the match, he's the victim instead. If both are, it's decided randomly!
They also wear their SMB3 colors if you've choosen Thwomp's third color!
</text>
</entry>
</xmsbt>